Full Specification
6.1 Instrument Entry Schema
Each entry has:

entry_id. A stable identifier.

library_id. Always instrument_library.

entry_schema_version. A semantic version.

identification. An object with:

name.

aliases. A list.

manufacturer.

model.

serial_number.

asset_tag.

classification. An object with:

type. One of the controlled vocabulary: spectrometer, interferometer, telescope, microscope, detector, sensor, gauge, balance, clock, laser, cryostat, magnet, particle_detector, camera, spectrograph, radiometer, other.

modality. One of: optical, infrared, ultraviolet, xray, gamma, radio, microwave, acoustic, seismic, thermal, electrical, magnetic, mechanical, chemical, biological, other.

domain. One of: astronomy, particle_physics, condensed_matter, chemistry, biology, medicine, geology, materials, metrology, other.

physical_principle. A free-text description of the measurement principle.

specifications. An object with:

range. An object with min, max, unit.

resolution. A value with unit.

accuracy. A value with unit and a statement of the reference.

precision. A value with unit.

sensitivity. A value with unit.

linearity. A value with unit or a percentage.

drift. A value with unit per time.

bandwidth. A value with unit.

sampling_rate. A value with unit.

operational_envelope. An object with:

temperature. min, max, unit.

pressure. min, max, unit.

humidity. min, max, unit.

voltage. min, max, unit.

magnetic_field. min, max, unit.

radiation. min, max, unit.

vibration. min, max, unit.

calibration. An array of calibration records. Each record has:

date.

standard. The reference standard used.

traceability_chain. A list of steps to a national metrology institute or a primary standard.

certificate. An identifier or a URL.

uncertainty. A value with unit.

uncertainty_budget. An array of budget items. Each item has:

mode. The measurement mode.

type_a. The type A contribution.

type_b. The type B contribution.

combined. The combined standard uncertainty.

expanded. The expanded uncertainty.

coverage_factor. The coverage factor k.

unit.

provenance. An object with:

depositor_id.

depositor_affiliation.

deposit_date.

source.

tool_version.

references. A list of DOIs or URLs.

keywords. A list.

notes. Free text.

moderation_status. pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. An entry ID or null.

superseded_by. An entry ID or null.

6.2 Controlled Vocabularies
The type vocabulary is: spectrometer, interferometer, telescope, microscope, detector, sensor, gauge, balance, clock, laser, cryostat, magnet, particle_detector, camera, spectrograph, radiometer, other.

The modality vocabulary is: optical, infrared, ultraviolet, xray, gamma, radio, microwave, acoustic, seismic, thermal, electrical, magnetic, mechanical, chemical, biological, other.

The domain vocabulary is: astronomy, particle_physics, condensed_matter, chemistry, biology, medicine, geology, materials, metrology, other.

The vocabularies are versioned and stored in the library registry.

6.3 The Search Engine
The search engine supports:

Search by name. Exact, prefix, fuzzy.

Search by type. Controlled vocabulary.

Search by domain. Controlled vocabulary.

Search by specification range. For example, resolution better than 1 nm.

Search by uncertainty threshold. For example, expanded uncertainty less than 0.1 percent.

Search by traceability. For example, traceable to NIST or PTB.

Search by depositor.

Search by date range.

Search by keywords.

The search engine uses the alias index, the type index, the domain index, the specification index, the uncertainty index, and the traceability index.

6.4 The Comparison Engine
The comparison engine takes two or more entry IDs and a field filter.

It returns a field-by-field table.

For each field, it shows the value for each instrument and a flag if the values differ.

The comparison is deterministic.

6.5 The Calibration Rules
A calibration record must have a date, a standard, a traceability chain, a certificate, and an uncertainty.

The traceability chain must terminate at a national metrology institute or a primary standard.

The chain is a list of steps, each with an institute, a standard, and a date.

6.6 The Uncertainty Rules
An uncertainty budget must have at least one item.

Each item must have a mode, a type A contribution, a type B contribution, a combined standard uncertainty, an expanded uncertainty, a coverage factor, and a unit.

The combined standard uncertainty is the root sum of squares of the type A and type B contributions.

The expanded uncertainty is the combined standard uncertainty times the coverage factor.

The default coverage factor is 2, corresponding to approximately 95 percent confidence for a normal distribution.

6.7 The Version Rules
Each entry has a version.

Each edit creates a new version.

The supersedes and superseded_by fields form a chain.

The chain must be acyclic.

The library has a version.

The library version increments when the schema or the controlled vocabularies change.

6.8 The Curation Rules
Approve. Set moderation_status to approved.

Reject. Set moderation_status to rejected.

Edit. Update the entry fields, keep the provenance, add a curation note, increment the version.

Each action records the moderator ID and the curation notes.

6.9 The Autofill Rules
The library registers with App 49 as instrument_library.

The entry type is instrument.

The autofill lookup matches on name, aliases, manufacturer, model, and serial number.

The autofill field filter supports returning only the identification fields, only the classification fields, only the specification fields, or any subset.

6.10 The Integration Rules
With App 23, instrument entries can be cited by physics claims.

With App 20, instrument annotations carry provenance.

With App 7, every edit is visible in the revision history.

With App 49, the library serves autofill lookups.

With App 3, entries can be exported as PROV-O.

With App 17, the schema is registered in the STAG Schema Library.

Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Submit Entry
function submitEntry(entry, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor").

Step 2. validateEntry(entry, instrumentSchema).

If invalid, return the validation errors.

Step 3. entryId = generateEntryId().

Set entry_id, deposit_date, depositor_id, depositor_affiliation, moderation_status pending, version 1.

Step 4. insertEntry(entry).

Step 5. updateAliasIndex.

Step 6. insertProvenance.

Step 7. insertAuditLog.

Step 8. return entry_id and status submitted.

7.2 Curate Entry
function curateEntry(entryId, action, curationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator").

Step 2. entry = selectEntry(entryId).

If null, return an error.

Step 3. If action is approve, set moderation_status approved.

If action is reject, set moderation_status rejected.

If action is edit, update entry fields, increment version, add a curation note.

Step 4. insertCurationRecord.

Step 5. insertAuditLog.

Step 6. return entry_id and status.

7.3 Search
function search(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader").

Step 2. candidates = selectCandidates(query).

Step 3. filtered = applyFilters(candidates, query).

Step 4. ranked = rankResults(filtered, query).

Step 5. paginated = paginate(ranked, query.page, query.page_size).

Step 6. return paginated.

7.4 Compare
function compare(entryIds, fieldFilter, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader").

Step 2. entries = selectEntries(entryIds).

Step 3. fields = fieldFilter or the union of all fields.

Step 4. table = buildComparisonTable(entries, fields).

Step 5. return table.

7.5 Uncertainty Computation
function computeUncertainty(budgetItems):

For each item:

combined = sqrt(typeA^2 + typeB^2).

expanded = combined * coverageFactor.

Return the items with the computed combined and expanded values.

7.6 Traceability Validation
function validateTraceability(chain):

The chain must be a non-empty list.

Each step must have an institute, a standard, and a date.

The last step must be a national metrology institute or a primary standard.

Return valid or the validation errors.

